<file path="backlog/tasks/bcc-2 - Make-the-doctor-hook-check-host-aware.md">
---
id: BCC-2
title: Make the doctor hook check host-aware
status: Done
assignee:
  - '@claude'
created_date: '2026-08-31 12:20'
updated_date: '2026-08-31 12:45'
labels: []
dependencies: []
priority: high
type: bug
ordinal: 2000
---

## Description

<!-- SECTION:DESCRIPTION:BEGIN -->
Under OMP the doctor always ends in `FAIL no hook has recorded a run for this session`. `collectDoctor` derives its session from `CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID` and falls back to the literal `cli`, an id nothing ever writes, so the hook record is always empty. OMP has no hook processes at all — the extension replaces them — so the check is meaningless there and the report contradicts its own session counters. Weaker models read the FAIL as a broken SessionStart hook and recommend `/backlog-md:setup`, which fixes nothing.
<!-- SECTION:DESCRIPTION:END -->

## Acceptance Criteria
<!-- AC:BEGIN -->
- [x] #1 With CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID set the hook line and its FAIL behave exactly as today
- [x] #2 Without CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID the report carries no hook line and instead reports newest session state and its age
- [x] #3 Without CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID and with no session state recorded the report FAILs naming the missing session state, not hooks
- [x] #4 The cache line never shows the cli.json fallback path in the non-Claude-Code host
- [x] #5 commands/doctor.md scopes its no-hook-recorded explanation to Claude Code
<!-- AC:END -->

## Implementation Plan

<!-- SECTION:PLAN:BEGIN -->
1. Drop the "cli" sessionId default in collectDoctor so an absent CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID means "not Claude Code".
2. Under Claude Code keep cache path, snapshot and hookRuns; under any other host skip all three and record extension liveness (newest of listSessions mtime and listSessionSummaries endedAt) instead.
3. formatDoctor prints the hook line only for the Claude Code host and an extension-liveness line otherwise, ok with an age or FAIL when nothing was ever recorded.
4. Scope the no-hook-recorded paragraph in commands/doctor.md to Claude Code and name the new extension line.
5. Tests: existing hook FAIL test stays green; add coverage for the extension-host ok and FAIL lines and for the absent cache line.
<!-- SECTION:PLAN:END -->

## Implementation Notes

<!-- SECTION:NOTES:BEGIN -->
collectDoctor no longer defaults sessionId; an absent CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID now means "not Claude Code" and skips the cache read, the snapshot and the hook check, reporting extension liveness (newest of listSessions mtime and listSessionSummaries endedAt) instead. Evidence: `node scripts/backlog-cc.mjs doctor` here ends in "FAIL no hook has recorded a run" (env var set); `env -u CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID node scripts/backlog-cc.mjs doctor` ends in "FAIL no session state recorded — the extension has not run in this repository" with no cache line. Unit tests: doctor.test.mjs, 38 pass, including the two new host cases and the unchanged Claude Code ones. Full suite 436 pass, biome and tsc clean.
<!-- SECTION:NOTES:END -->

## Final Summary

<!-- SECTION:FINAL_SUMMARY:BEGIN -->
The hook check is now host-aware: Claude Code keeps the cache path, snapshot and hookRuns line unchanged, every other host gets one extension-liveness line instead — ok with the age of the newest session state, FAIL when nothing was ever recorded. The cli.json fallback session is gone, so the report can no longer diagnose a session nobody writes. commands/doctor.md scopes the old explanation to Claude Code and names the new line. Verified by running the doctor with and without CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID and by four unit tests in test/unit/doctor.test.mjs.
<!-- SECTION:FINAL_SUMMARY:END -->
</file>

