id: BCC-6
title: Distinguish native OMP commands from their file duplicates
status: Done
assignee:
  - '@claude'
created_date: '2026-08-31 12:21'
updated_date: '2026-08-31 12:45'
labels: []
dependencies: []
priority: low
type: enhancement
ordinal: 6000
---

## Description

<!-- SECTION:DESCRIPTION:BEGIN -->
Under OMP every slash command appears twice in autocomplete: the extension registration via pi.registerCommand and the prompt template that OMPs Claude-plugin provider reads from commands/*.md. Only the native one ever executes — OMP resolves extension commands before file commands — and the duplication cannot be removed, because both hosts read the same .claude-plugin/plugin.json and OMP does not substitute ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT} in command bodies, so the file variant must not win. Remaining work is confusion protection and documentation only.
<!-- SECTION:DESCRIPTION:END -->

## Acceptance Criteria
<!-- AC:BEGIN -->
- [x] #1 The natively registered command carries a description that distinguishes it from the file variant in the picker
- [x] #2 A contract test reads commands/ from disk and fails when a command has no native registration
- [x] #3 The README explains the duplication and that both entries lead to the same execution
<!-- AC:END -->

## Implementation Plan

<!-- SECTION:PLAN:BEGIN -->
1. Append a marker to the natively registered command description in omp/index.mjs so the picker shows which of the two rows executes.
2. Strengthen the existing commands/ contract test to compare the directory against the registrations the extension actually makes, not against a hardcoded list.
3. Extend the README OMP install paragraph with the duplication and its outcome.
<!-- SECTION:PLAN:END -->

## Implementation Notes

<!-- SECTION:NOTES:BEGIN -->
The native registration appends "(native)" to each command description. The existing directory test now also instantiates the extension and compares its registered command names against the files in commands/, so a new command file without a native registration fails there rather than only against the hardcoded COMMAND_NAMES list; it also asserts the marker on every description. README gained a paragraph in the OMP install section. 23 contract tests pass, 436 in the suite.
<!-- SECTION:NOTES:END -->

## Final Summary

<!-- SECTION:FINAL_SUMMARY:BEGIN -->
The two picker entries are now distinguishable: the extension registration carries "(native)" in its description, the Markdown file variant does not. The contract test derives the expected registrations from the commands/ directory itself, so a command that would exist only in the broken file variant fails the build. The README explains why the duplication cannot be removed and that both entries run the same native handler.
<!-- SECTION:FINAL_SUMMARY:END -->
</file>

