Four documentation defects. (E1) commands/doctor.md carries 48 lines of instruction; MiniMax-M3 ran the diagnosis twice and explained one FAIL line across three paragraphs, losing the "one consequence and one fix per FAIL line" instruction. (E2) The README quotes a global Claude Code install as "9 Skills, ~369 tokens always-on"; the plugin ships exactly one skill, skills/backlog-workflow, measured earlier at ~60 always-on / ~800 on-invoke — the quoted figure came from a whole config directory including foreign plugins. (E3) The per-event hook process cost under Claude Code (32-70ms, essentially Node startup) is undocumented, so the project-scoped install should be named the lossless choice there while a global install stays harmless under OMP. (E4) Prewalk hands off to a faster model mid-session, so that sessions counters belong to no single model; eval/run.mjs already passes --no-prewalk, the doctor does not.
<!-- SECTION:DESCRIPTION:END -->

## Acceptance Criteria
<!-- AC:BEGIN -->
- [x] #1 commands/doctor.md is shorter and prescribes the output shape unambiguously, with one consequence and one fix per FAIL line
- [x] #2 The README skill-cost figure is re-measured against an installation without foreign plugins and corrected
- [x] #3 The README recommends project scope under Claude Code and states why global scope is harmless under OMP
- [x] #4 The README records prewalk model mixing as a known limitation of counters outside the evaluator
<!-- AC:END -->

## Implementation Plan

<!-- SECTION:PLAN:BEGIN -->
1. Rewrite commands/doctor.md: one run, a prescribed report shape, and one line per warn and FAIL — including the new extension line from BCC-2.
2. E2: re-measure the figure in a Claude Code config directory holding no other plugin, and correct the README to whatever that measurement says.
3. E3: name the project-scoped install as the lossless choice under Claude Code, with the per-event process cost already in the cost table, and say why global scope is harmless under OMP.
4. E4: record prewalk model mixing as a limitation of counters read outside the evaluator.
<!-- SECTION:PLAN:END -->

## Implementation Notes

<!-- SECTION:NOTES:BEGIN -->
AC #1: commands/doctor.md is 44 lines / 2178 bytes, down from 48 / 2463, while covering two more FAIL lines (the BCC-2 extension line and the registered-but-gone install). The instruction part now prescribes one run and one line per warn and FAIL, in order, with no summary and no second run.
AC #3 and #4: README gained a paragraph on the per-event process floor under Claude Code and why OMP does not pay it, and a Limitations bullet on prewalk splitting a session across two models. test/unit/readme.test.mjs passes; suite 436 pass.

AC #2 is NOT met and cannot be met as written: the quoted figure ("9 Skills, ~369 tokens always-on") appears nowhere in README.md, in any other file of this repository, or in its git history (`git log -S369`, `git grep 369` both empty). There is no README number to correct — the figure most likely came from a host readout over a whole config directory. What could be done from here was done: the README now states the actual prompt-side cost of this package (one skill, skills/backlog-workflow, 3.4 KB, plus the two OMP rules). A real token measurement needs a Claude Code installation with no foreign plugins, which cannot be produced from this repository.

Correction to the AC #2 note above: it was wrong. Measured today in a throwaway CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR holding no other plugin, "claude plugin details backlog-md" reports "Skills (9)" — backlog-workflow plus the eight commands, which Claude Code counts as skills — and "Always-on: ~369 tok". The figure is this package alone, not a foreign-plugin artefact, and it is right. Independent confirmation from a recording Anthropic endpoint: the same session costs 74770 bytes with the plugin at user scope against 73107 with it disabled (+1663) in a repository without backlog/, and 75147 against 73099 (+2048) with one. Under OMP the same package costs +907 / +1163 system-prompt bytes.

The README paragraph written under the wrong finding ("one skill, 3.4 KB, plus two OMP rules") understated it and has been replaced by the measured numbers for both hosts, which also strengthen the project-scope recommendation from AC #3.

Validation: npm test 436 pass / 0 fail after the README rewrite (test/unit/readme.test.mjs included).
